==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*after}}, {{m|gem-pro|*aftiri||more aft, further behind}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sv}} {{m|ine-pro|*apotero||further behind, further away}}, comparative form of {{m|ine-pro|*apo-||off, behind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛfˌtɛr/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-efter.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Preposition===
{{head|sv|preposition}}

# [[after]]; subsequent; later in time than ''or'' later in a sequence than
# [[by]]; using the rules or logic of
# [[by]]; ''as in'' one by one, one after another
#: ''en '''efter''' en''
#:: ''one by one''
# [[as to]]; in a manner conforming or corresponding to
#: ''Sortera dem '''efter''' storlek och färg.''
#:: ''Sort them as to size and color.''

====Related terms====
* [[därefter]]
* [[efterhand]]
* [[efterklok]]
